  "solution": [
    "An exterior angle of a triangle equals the sum of the two interior angles that are not next to it.",
    "\\(125 = 50 + x\\), so \\(x = 75\\).",
    "Check: angle \\(ACB = 180 - 125 = 55^{\\circ}\\), and \\(50 + 75 + 55 = 180\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "P=figure['points']\nd=lambda a,b: sqrt((P[a][0]-P[b][0])**2+(P[a][1]-P[b][1])**2)\nang=lambda a,v,b: N(acos(((P[a][0]-P[v][0])*(P[b][0]-P[v][0])+(P[a][1]-P[v][1])*(P[b][1]-P[v][1]))/(d(a,v)*d(b,v)))*180/pi)\nassert P['B'][1]==P['C'][1]==P['D'][1]\nassert abs(ang('A','C','D')-125)<0.1 and abs(ang('B','A','C')-50)<0.1\nans=125-50\nassert abs(ang('A','B','C')-ans)<0.1\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans==75\n",
